      "message": "Weirdly, fizz has the #define the other way around.\nAll the other boards have a number for the CONFIG_CHARGER_MIN_POWER_MW_FOR_POWER_ON #define,\nso maybe the fizz pattern should be followed.\nI don\u0027t know the exact meaning of these #defines and how they are different.\nMy quick scan of where they are used seem to indicate that CONFIG_CHARGER_MIN_POWER_MW_FOR_POWER_ON represents the minimum power required before the AP gets turned on, and PD_OPERATING_POWER_MW indicates how much power is required before USB power delivery is enabled? So it would seem clearer to have a real number for CONFIG_CHARGER_MIN_POWER_MW_FOR_POWER_ON.",
